WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.997
On the federal side, change
control calls for the

2
00:00:02.997 --> 00:00:06.238
evidence attachment and hash
on every closed record.

3
00:00:06.238 --> 00:00:10.074
Control verification calls for
the re-read result and its time.

4
00:00:10.074 --> 00:00:15.338
Continuous monitoring calls for counts of
closed and reopened records each period.

5
00:00:15.338 --> 00:00:19.413
Audit record generation calls for
the verifier account's audit trail.

6
00:00:19.413 --> 00:00:23.694
To validate, the kit's tests prove
that a dry run writes nothing,

7
00:00:23.694 --> 00:00:28.563
that a match closes, that a mismatch
reopens, and that a stale read waits.

8
00:00:28.563 --> 00:00:33.006
On a live system, a person's close
should land in awaiting verification,

9
00:00:33.006 --> 00:00:36.837
and only the client should close
it, once the account matches.

10
00:00:36.837 --> 00:00:42.412
The re-read uses SailPoint's account and
search A P I's and Graph's users endpoint.

11
00:00:42.412 --> 00:00:45.551
GCC High uses its own Graph host.

12
00:00:45.551 --> 00:00:50.250
Until the client runs on a schedule,
the verifier runs it by hand once a day.

13
00:00:50.250 --> 00:00:52.580
To roll back, disable the business rule,

14
00:00:52.580 --> 00:00:55.700
though closures lose their
evidence while it's off.
